                <pb facs="0768" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 2/275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-14T09:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                                1925—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 14—9:33
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Department’s telegraphic instructions Nos. 4, February 7, 3 p.m., and 7,
                    February 12, 4 p.m. I am delivering to Persian Government today note on opium
                    containing substance of first-mentioned telegram as modified. My British
                    colleague has been notified of action I am taking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
